## SQ-CBW-01 | wood cutting board recipes on the plank tags; board tags
@group A
@commands Boot; grep `latest.log` for `could not add the stone and wood cutting boards` and `invalid for block`; recipe dump `creativedelight:shaped/oak_cutting_board` (and the other 7), `creativedelight:shaped/cutting_board`; check `farmersdelight:cutting_board` recipe id is gone; tag probe `#creativedelight:cutting_board_planks`, `#minecraft:mineable/axe`, `#creativeengineering:counter_toppers`, `#creativeengineering:hammer_no_rotate`
@pass No log line; 8 wood recipes (2 sticks + 4 of that wood's planks) plus the spruce board's on `#creativedelight:cutting_board_planks`; that tag holds spruce and modded / vertical / polished planks but none of the 8 vanilla planks; the 8 boards in the three block tags
@fails `allowExtraBoards` not run; `addMatching` except not applied (the tag then still has oak planks: two recipes match oak)
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootreject could not add the stone and wood cutting boards|invalid for block
> cdevtest recipes _cutting_board
> cdevtest recipes farmersdelight:cutting_board
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:shaped/oak_cutting_board
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:shaped/cutting_board
> cdevtest tag item creativedelight:cutting_board_planks
> cdevtest tag block minecraft:mineable/axe
> cdevtest tag block creativedelight:counter_toppers
> cdevtest tag block creativedelight:hammer_no_rotate
waitlog verb=tag kind=block tag=creativedelight:hammer_no_rotate n= 20
count creativedelight:shaped/(oak|spruce|birch|jungle|acacia|dark_oak|mangrove|crimson|warped)_cutting_board -> >= 8
expect verb=recipes text=farmersdelight:cutting_board n=0
reject verb=tag kind=item tag=creativedelight:cutting_board_planks n=\d+ ids=.*minecraft:(oak|birch|jungle|acacia|dark_oak|mangrove|crimson|warped)_planks
look oak board = 2 sticks + 4 oak planks (each wood's own planks); shaped/cutting_board (spruce board) on #creativedelight:cutting_board_planks, which holds spruce and modded / vertical / polished planks; the 8 wood boards in mineable/axe, counter_toppers and hammer_no_rotate (tags moved from creativeengineering: to creativedelight:). Spruce board's own id is the plain farmersdelight:cutting_board
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-CBW-02 | oak and crimson boards cut raw beef with a knife, drop themselves with or without an axe
@group A
@commands Place `farmersdelight:oak_cutting_board` and `crimson_cutting_board`; `/data get block`; fake player right-clicks a carrot then a knife; break each with and without an axe; reload the chunk
@pass Each has a `farmersdelight:cutting_board` block entity, cuts the carrot, drops itself both ways, keeps its item over the reload
@fails as SQ-FCB-07
@from batches/r1113/fix_c2a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> setblock 300 -60 360 farmersdelight:oak_cutting_board[facing=north]
> setblock 302 -60 360 farmersdelight:crimson_cutting_board[facing=north]
> pbot hold c2b minecraft:beef 1
> pbot use c2b 300 -60 360
> pbot hold c2b farmersdelight:iron_knife 1
> pbot use c2b 300 -60 360
> pbot hold c2b minecraft:beef 1
> pbot use c2b 302 -60 360
> pbot hold c2b farmersdelight:iron_knife 1
> pbot use c2b 302 -60 360
sleep 2
> cdevtest inv 300 -60 360
> cdevtest inv 302 -60 360
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=296,y=-62,z=356,dx=10,dy=6,dz=8]
> cdevtest break 300 -60 360
> cdevtest break 302 -60 360 held=minecraft:iron_axe
> setblock 300 -60 360 farmersdelight:oak_cutting_board[facing=north]
> setblock 302 -60 360 farmersdelight:crimson_cutting_board[facing=north]
> cdevtest break 300 -60 360 held=minecraft:iron_axe
> cdevtest break 302 -60 360
count verb=inv via=\S+ slots=\d+ filled=0 == 2
count verb=break who=\S+ broken=true == 4
count verb=break drops=farmersdelight:(oak|crimson)_cutting_board:1 stacks= == 4
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the beef left both boards after the knife use (filled=0), the kill line removed the cut result items (minced beef, farmersdelight:cutting/beef) before the breaks; each break drops 1 of its own board, bare hand and axe
> clear c2b

## SQ-CBW-03 | rerun: a pumpkin pie goes on a birch board sitting on a CfB counter; no pie block placed
@group A
@commands `/setblock` a CfB counter, a `birch_cutting_board` and a `granite_cutting_board` on two counters; fake player places a vanilla pumpkin pie on the birch board
@pass Pie not placed on the board (it stays in hand or goes on top as FD's board allows); no error in the log
@fails `FDBackportEvents` check
@from batches/r1115/p4_a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> setblock 304 -60 360 cookingforblockheads:counter[facing=north]
> setblock 306 -60 360 cookingforblockheads:counter[facing=north]
> setblock 304 -59 360 farmersdelight:birch_cutting_board[facing=north]
> setblock 306 -59 360 farmersdelight:granite_cutting_board[facing=north]
> pbot hold c2b minecraft:pumpkin_pie 1
> pbot use c2b 304 -59 360 up
sleep 1
> cdevtest state 304 -59 360
> cdevtest inv 304 -59 360
> cdevtest state 304 -58 360
> cdevtest player c2b
reject Exception
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
expect verb=state pos=304,-58,360 state=minecraft:air
expect verb=player name=c2b .*main=empty
look board inv: the pie on the board or not placed as FD's board allows (pass: not placed as a block on the board); the bot no longer holds the pie if the board took it
> clear c2b
> pbot remove c2b
> pbot remove G

